GAL20RA10
SPI CTRL

/PL  NC  NC  NC /dBRST CLK E    MISO  /RST    NC   NC GND
/OE /C0 /C1 /C2 /BRST  NC  SCLK MISOr /OUTPUT srS1 NC VCC

; SPI Clock
SCLK        =   /CLK *  dBRST

; Retimed MISO value
MISOr.R     =   /RST *  MISO
MISOr.CLK   =   /CLK

; Burst - 8 SPI clock cycles
BRST.R      =   /RST *  E    * /OUTPUT * /C2 * /C1 * /C0
              + /RST *  BRST * /C2
              + /RST *  BRST * /C1
              + /RST *  BRST * /C0
/BRST.CLK   =    CLK

; OUTPUT - waiting for E to go low; allow read of value
OUTPUT.R    =   /RST *  E *  OUTPUT
              + /RST *  E *  BRST *  C2 *  C1 *  C0
/OUTPUT.CLK =    CLK

; Shift register S1
srS1        =   /OUTPUT * /BRST

; SPI cycle counter
C0.R        =   /RST *  BRST * /C0

C1.R        =   /RST *  BRST * /C1 *  C0
              + /RST *  BRST *  C1 * /C0

C2.R        =   /RST *  BRST *  C2 * /C1
              + /RST *  BRST *  C2 * /C0
              + /RST *  BRST * /C2 *  C1 *  C0

/C0.CLK     =    CLK
/C1.CLK     =    CLK
/C2.CLK     =    CLK


DESCRIPTION

Control logic for bidirectional SPI interface

Inputs:
  CLK           System clock Phi2
  E             Enable send - start sending. If still asserted when burst complete then output data
  MISO          MISO input for retiming
 /RST           Active low synchronous reset signal
 /dBRST         Delayed BRST signal to avoid runt pulse on the SCLK output which might otherwise
                occur when the burst on SCLK begins - BRST goes high on the edge that /CLK falls 

Outputs:
  SCLK          The SPI clock
  MISOr         The retimed MISO signal, clocked on SCLK
 /BRST          The negated BRST signal (SCLK active) for feeding back to the input for gating
                /CLK to generate SCLK
 /OUTPUT        When low, received value is output until E goes low
                Controls shift register S0 (see below)
                Controls shift register active low output enable to allow reading received value
  srS1          Along with WAITsrS0OE, control S0 and S1 inputs for the 74HC922 shift register:
                S0 S1
                 0  0 Hold value (hold for reading)
                 1  1 Load value (parallel load - on every CLK while idle
                 1  0 Shifting value for output on every CLK

Intermediate values:
 /C0, /C1, /C2  Counter values for the 8 clock steps
 /BRST          Burst not active (active low since device resets with value high)

